DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Function eellff__mmeemmoorryy() is used to process an ELF file or ar(1) archive
     whose image is present in memory.

     Argument _i_m_a_g_e points to the start of the memory image of the file or ar‐
     chive.  Argument _s_i_z_e contains the size in bytes of the memory image.

     The ELF descriptor is created for reading (i.e., analogous to the use of
     elf_begin(3) with a command argument value of ELF_C_READ).

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Function eellff__mmeemmoorryy() returns a pointer to a new ELF descriptor if suc‐
     cessful, or NULL if an error occurred.

     The return value may be queried for the file type using elf_kind(3).

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     To read parse an elf file, use:

           int fd;
           void *p;
           struct stat sb;
           Elf *e;
           ...
           if ((fd = open("./elf-file", O_RDONLY)) < 0 ||
               fstat(fd, &sb) < 0 ||
               (p = mmap(NULL, sb.st_size, PROT_READ, MAP_PRIVATE, fd, (off_t) 0)) ==
               MAP_FAILED) {
                   ... handle system error ...
           }

           if ((e = elf_memory(p, sb.st_size)) == NULL) {
                   ... handle elf(3) error ...
           }
           ... use ELF descriptor "e" here ...

EERRRROORRSS
     Function eellff__mmeemmoorryy() can fail with the following errors:

     [ELF_E_ARGUMENT]  A NULL value was used for argument _i_m_a_g_e or the value
                       of argument _s_z was zero.

     [ELF_E_HEADER]    The header of the ELF object contained an unsupported
                       value in its _e___i_d_e_n_t_[_E_I___C_L_A_S_S_] field.

     [ELF_E_HEADER]    The header of the ELF object contained an unsupported
                       value in its _e___i_d_e_n_t_[_E_I___D_A_T_A_] field.

     [ELF_E_RESOURCE]  An out of memory condition was detected.

     [ELF_E_SEQUENCE]  Function eellff__mmeemmoorryy() was called before a working ver‐
                       sion was set using elf_version(3).

     [ELF_E_VERSION]   The ELF object referenced by argument _i_m_a_g_e was of an
                       unsupported ELF version.

